Please answer the following questions: Hydroxy acid $\mathrm{HO}-\left(\mathrm{CH}_{2}\right)_{4}-\mathrm{COOH}$ undergoes linear polycondensation, and the measured weight-average molecular weight of the product is $18400 \mathrm{~g}/\mathrm{mol}$. Calculate:  
(1) The percentage of carboxylic groups that have been esterified;  
(2) The number-average degree of polymerization ($\bar{X}_{n}$);  
(3) The number of structural units.

target:
(1) Given $\bar{M}_{w}=18400$, $M_{0}=100$:  
$\bar{X}_{w}=\frac{\bar{M}_{w}}{M_{0}}=\frac{18400}{100}=184$;  
$\bar{X}_{w}=\frac{(1+p)}{(1-p)}$;  
$p=\frac{\left(X_{w}-1\right)}{\left(X_{w}+1\right)}=\frac{(184-1)}{(184+1)}=0.989$;  
Thus, the percentage of hydroxyl groups esterified is $98.9\%$.  

(2) Based on $\frac{\bar{M}_{w}}{\bar{M}_{n}}=1+p=1+0.989=1.989$:  
$\bar{M}_{n}=\frac{18400}{1.989}=9251$;  
$\bar{X}_{n}=\frac{\bar{M}_{n}}{M_{0}}=\frac{9251}{100}=92.51$.  

(3) The number of structural units = $X_{n} = 92.51$.

(1)$\Delta\mathrm{G}^{0\prime}=-\mathrm{RT} \ln K_{\mathrm{d}}=35.9\mathrm{~kJ}/\mathrm{mol}$;  
(2)$K_{\mathrm{a}}=\frac{1}{K_{\mathrm{d}}}=2 \times 10^{6} \mathrm{~mol}^{-1} \mathrm{~L}$;  
(3) Assuming the rate constant for releasing the hapten is $k_{1}$ and the binding rate constant is $k_{2}$,  
by $K_{\mathrm{d}}=\frac{k_{1}}{k_{2}}$,  
then the binding rate constant $k_{2}=\frac{k_{1}}{K_{\mathrm{d}}}=\frac{120}{\left(5 \times 10^{-7}\right)}=2.4\times10^{8}\left(\mathrm{~mol}^{-1} \cdot \mathrm{s}^{-1}\cdot\mathrm{L}\right)$,  
this value is close to the diffusion-controlled limit for small molecule-protein binding $\left(10^{8}\right.~\mathrm{to}~\left.10^{9} \mathrm{~mol}^{-1} \cdot \mathrm{s}^{-1} \cdot \mathrm{L}\right)$.

The average relative molecular weight of the oil = $1000 \div (210 \div 56) \times 3 = 800$;  
The moles of $100~\mathrm{g}$ of oil = $(100 \div 800)~\mathrm{mol} = 0.125~\mathrm{mol}$;  
The average number of double bonds per molecule of oil = $68 \div (126.9 \times 2) \div 0.125 = 2$.

